Subject: [PATCH 1/2] WP-0.9, labels as strong as the content (cld-advisor's
 series 1, patch 1; built on 323f92327 with series 2, 3 and 4 of WP-0.7
 applied): THE GRADE OF A VERDICT IS HELD TO THE EVIDENCE IT NAMES (the
 audit's M1: PROVED means at least five things). A verdict file says PROVED,
 NEGATIVE, OPEN or RETRACTED, and nothing of what kind of support the word
 has. Of 1,592 verdict files none carries such a field. THE FIELD: grade, one
 of the programme's five words (theorem, exact computation, numerical
 estimate, sealed cells held, process), and grade_evidence, the files of the
 arc it rests on. THE GATE is arc-data, which already holds the arcs' data to
 itself; no gate is added. Where a grade stands: the word is one of the five;
 every file it names is in the tree; and the files are of the kind the word
 asks. A theorem names a lock of its own in which an assert can fail. An exact
 computation names its script and such a lock. A numerical estimate names its
 script and the committed output of it. Sealed cells held names its sealed
 file, and grade_cells as held and sealed, with held no more than sealed. A
 process names nothing. The evidence is the arc's own: under its folder, or a
 lock in tests/ that carries its number. WHO MUST CARRY ONE: the arcs the
 candidate runs on, fourteen by main's measurement in B1888. That list is
 typed in the gates' file and its lock holds it to main's own file; it is
 computed when the graph of WP-0.12 stands. None of the fourteen carries a
 grade today, so all fourteen are held by name as owing one, and the list may
 only shrink; an arc of the chain with no grade that is not named fails. No
 verdict file is changed by this patch, and no arc is graded by it: a grade is
 a judgement on an arc's content, and it is main's. What it does not reach:
 the gate reads a form. That a lock can fail does not make it a proof of the
 claim; that a script and an output are named does not make the estimate
 sound; the count of cells held is the arc's own word. The five words are not
 the nine labels of how a result was checked. The lock:
 tests/test_a_grade_is_held_to_its_evidence.py, seven tests, eleven ways a
 grade says more than its evidence; on the commit before, six fail and the
 control holds. Tested against planted errors, 11 of 11 ways; computed once. 0
 of 19.

